            <div xml:id="d702">

                <pb facs="0866" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/2629: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-12T12:00:00-05:00">April 12,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. Reference Legation’s telegram No. 40, April 8, 1 p.m., could the Department
                    telegraph its decision concerning the confirmation <pb facs="0867" n="779"
                        xml:id="pg779"/> of the Financial Adviser’s powers through exchange of notes
                    as early as possible as the budget must be deposited within 48 hours and the
                    Financial Adviser cannot give his accord until a decision is reached on this
                    point.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
